{
  "summary": "This experiment replaced the scVI_n200 RNA encoder with scGPT in the RNA-only, multiprofile, avgpool setting (a single-variable swap from llm_summary_006), to test whether a different learned encoder captures complementary gene-expression structure in the highest-impact configuration. The validation accuracy of 0.530 (F1 0.515) is substantially below the scVI multiprofile result (0.650, F1 0.628) and only marginally above the singleprofile scVI baseline (0.520, F1 0.498), indicating that the ~13% multiprofile aggregation gain observed with scVI is largely absent when using scGPT. It remains uncertain whether this gap reflects a fundamental limitation of scGPT's learned representation for this task, a dimensionality or hyperparameter mismatch, or run-to-run variability, and whether scGPT might perform differently under alternative aggregation strategies or multimodal configurations."
}

